      "formation": "Sleipner / Skagerrak Formation",
      "mudWeight": 1.25,
      "summary": "Run SBT log. Rig down wireline.",
      "activities": "00:00 - 01:00: PU shooting nipple and RIH with same on 7\" casing to 92 m.\n01:00 - 02:30: Installed XO sub for wireline shieve on top drive saver sub. Changed to 45 ft bails.\n02:30 - 03:30: Western atlas made up SBT CCL GR.\n03:30 - 04:30: Western atlas investigated power failure on logging tool. Changed out swivel and MU new connection.\n04:30 - 05:00: PU casing joint with XO sub and stuffing box. Connected logging cable.\n05:00 - 06:00: Western atlas had indication of periodical failure on logging tool. Changed out cable head.\n06:00 - 06:30: RIH with SBT-CCL-GR to 65 m. MU last casing joint. Positioned string with heave compensator and closed lower annular.\n06:30 - 10:00: Western/atlas RIH with SBT-CCL-GR. Tool stood up at 1270 m. Worked tool down. Stood up again at 1440 m. Tried to work through no success.\n10:00 - 12:30: POOH with wireline. Disconnected upper casing joint and LD logging tool.\n12:30 - 14:30: Installed wts tools below SBT to allow for more weight.\n14:30 - 17:00: Tool check showed failure on vdl section. Changed to back up tool. Performed new toolcheck. OK. RIH to 150 m and installed upper casing joint.\n17:00 - 23:00: RIH with SBT-CCL-GR. Checked pick up weight at 1000 m 2500 lbs 2000 m 3600 lbs 2500 m 5600 lbs. At 3000 m pick up weight was 8000 lbs, logging weight was 7500 lbs. At 3500 m we showed PUW lw 8000 7500 lbs. At TD 4036 m wireline depth we showed PUW lw 10000 9500 lbs.\n23:00 - 00:00: Logged from 3993 m to 3556 m.\n",
      "sourceDataset": "Equinor Volve Open Data",
      "sourcePath": "Daily_Drilling_Reports/15/9-19 A/1997-10-08.pdf",
      "verified": true,
